it's a remarkable personal story but  what was behind the deal that bought  nazanin home and what could it mean for  future relations with iran so this is  the number that matters today just shy  of 400 million pounds the amount  transferred from the uk to iran  restricted for humanitarian purposes but  why well it comes down to historic debt  over this 1  750 tanks iran ordered and paid for them  all the way back in the 70s but the uk  never completed the order now it's a  hugely significant breakthrough but is  it going to herald a broader thawing of  relations well the key to that probably  lies here talks in vienna to try and  salvage the iran nuclear deal remember  it fell apart in 2018 when the u.s  withdrew under donald trump it hinges on  iran agreeing to reduce its capacity to  develop nuclear weapons in exchange for  the removal of harsh economic sanctions  this is why it matters so much to the  west this is stockpiles of enriched  uranium in iran the stuff needed to  develop that weapon just look at how it  fell right off after that deal was  struck but after the u.s left it started  to rack up again given the current  threat from russia this now matters more  than ever but there would also be huge  benefits to iran just look at what  happened to its economy after that deal  was struck in 2015 gdp that red line  started growing inflation came down but  after the u.s left the very opposite  happened the economy started to contract  an inflation look all the way up there  surging nearly 40 percent sanctions also  prevented iran from selling it's oil  freely again look after the deal was  struck production and exports both up  and after the u.s withdrew and those  sanctions started to bite it's really  fallen off now this matters for both  iran and the west oil is one of the  bedrocks of the iranian economy and it  won't have escaped anyone's attention  that the uk and others will now be  looking for new places to buy after  recently committing to not buying oil  from russia so could iran plug part of  that gap well in supply terms it's  certainly possible look at this iran has  the third largest proved reserves of oil  in the world after saudi arabia and  venezuela the only two countries ahead  and we know that the prime minister is  already courting other sellers this is  him today in fact he's traveled to the  uae and saudi arabia to help shore up  some of that global supply there would  of course be other obstacles to  repairing relations with iran not least  human rights and regional politics but  nazanin returning home is a huge  breakthrough a further thawing could  benefit both sides
 

